# SIMP 6.7.0 / RHEL 9.8 -- EL9 component pin set
#
# Generated for the RHEL 9 release effort (branch 6.7.0-RHEL-9.8).
# Base: upstream simp-core master @ 7f1409b, Puppetfile.pinned (EL8/6.6.0-2 era).
#
# SELECTION POLICY
#   Each component is pinned to its newest tag that declares EL9 support.
#   Where no tag declares EL9, the newest tag is used and annotated inline.
#
#   Upper version bounds in module metadata.json are NOT treated as binding.
#   They are release-time bookkeeping that lags reality: SIMP's own CI
#   (see any module's .fixtures.yml) tests every component against the
#   DEFAULT BRANCH of its dependencies, not against these bounds. Example:
#   haveged 0.15.0 (2024-09) caps simplib < 5.0.0, while simplib 7.0.1
#   (2026-08) is the current EL9 release and is what CI actually exercises.
#   Honouring those bounds would demote simplib to a non-EL9 version.
#
#   Known stale bounds are catalogued in docs/el9-stale-version-bounds.md
#   and are handled at RPM-build time via build/rpm/dependencies.yaml.
#

# EL9 FORKS
#   Some components carry EL9 fixes that upstream has not taken. Those are
#   maintained as forks of the exact upstream tag, with each fix as its own
#   commit, tagged <upstream-version>-el9. The diff against upstream is
#   deliberately minimal so the changes stay reviewable and submittable as PRs.
#
#   SIMP_EL9_FORK_BASE selects where they are fetched from. It defaults to the
#   local path used by the disconnected build host; point it at the GitLab RHEL9
#   project once that exists and nothing else here has to change:
#
#     export SIMP_EL9_FORK_BASE='https://gitlab.n3bulasystems.com/<group>/rhel9'
#
el9_fork_base = ENV['SIMP_EL9_FORK_BASE'] || 'file:///build/el9-forks/git'

# TWO COMPONENTS ARE PINNED BY COMMIT, NOT TAG
#   simp-adapter and rubygem-simp-cli carry their OpenVox/EL9 support only
#   on master; their newest tags (2.1.1 and 7.0.0/2021) predate OpenVox
#   entirely. Both are essential to the EL9 install path, so they are
#   pinned to reviewed SHAs. Re-pin to tags once upstream cuts releases.
#
moduledir 'src'

mod 'simp-doc',
  :git => 'https://github.com/simp/simp-doc',
  :branch => 'master'

moduledir 'src/assets'

